items.what:
A numpy BaselineImputer following D's frozen rules:
- covariance from pairwise-complete moments on the training fold, turned into a correlation and shrunk as R <- 0.9R + 0.1I, with eigenvalues floored at 1e-3;
- each test row's hidden|isna numeric cells filled with E[x_m | x_o] in the frame's z-space;
- categorical columns filled with the training mode.
Add a pre-registered clip to each column's training [min, max] as the range guard. Score it with recompute_folds(variant, seed, 5, 0.2, [], fold_scorer=factory) and score_baselines, then pair fold by fold against the model's K readout.

items.expected_outcome:
From probe D (3-seed means, tie band 0.003). condexp sets the bar on these induced variants:
- vehicle_20nan: 0.451 vs lgbm 0.473 (3/3 seeds);
- vehicle_60nan: 0.697 vs hgb 0.701 (3/3);
- spambase_60nan: 0.975 vs hgb 0.984 (3/3);
- credit-g_60nan: 0.988 vs mean_mode 1.000 (3/3). This is also marginally below the model's 0.992 (by 0.004, 2/3 seeds), so read it as marginal, not a verdict.

On masked cells it is below the bar on vehicle_20nan (0.478 vs 0.505), vehicle_60nan, spambase_60nan (0.956 vs 0.982), credit-g_40nan (0.990 vs 0.997) and credit-g_60nan.

It never beats the model beyond the tie band except the marginal credit-g_60nan, and on credit-g_80nan, where the model already loses to mean_mode.

Where it is weak:
- it blows up on heavy-tailed kc2 (1.23-1.28 unclipped);
- it is far behind on letter, pendigits and electricity (0.55-0.88 against bars of 0.35-0.69);
- on kr-vs-kp it equals mean_mode exactly, since that table is all categorical.

items.what:
D's arm:
- centre each column on its training mean;
- hard-impute a rank-k SVD on the training fold (start at 0, at most 100 iterations, tolerance 1e-5);
- with loadings W = V_k diag(s_k)/sqrt(n), fill each test row's gaps by the PPCA posterior z = (W_o'W_o + s2 I)^-1 W_o'(x_o - mu_o), where s2 is the mean of the discarded eigenvalues;
- fill categorical columns with the training mode.
Replace D's rank rule, which fails on spambase, with a rule fixed before scoring, e.g. a 90% energy share with no p//2 cap, or a ridge-regularised projection. Pre-register it.

items.gap_exposed:
It closes item 1's holes:
- real lgbm in place of the hgb proxy on E35;
- lgbm on the 5 variants that lack it on 101/202/303;
- paired missForest verdicts on E35's seeds.
It also turns probe D's means into paired verdicts with the fork's rule.

items.what:
Write datasets/generate_mnar.py beside generate_splits.py. It writes <base>_probit_60nan.csv for biodeg, kc2 and vehicle. These tables are all-numeric, so no categorical rule is needed. Each column hides exactly round(n*p) cells, the MCAR sibling's count, by weighted sampling with weights proportional to Phi(lambda_j x_j - c), large values hidden. Either use raw x_j with lambda_j = 1/(2 sigma_j), or z_j with 0.5, not both. Pre-register c.

Arms on seeds 42/7/13, 5 folds:
- G: defaults + --decode_checkpoint loss + --score_induced_checkpoint (the E35 recipe);
- M: --decode_gap_token null --decode_checkpoint loss --score_column_wise --score_induced_checkpoint (the E31 shape).
Run both on the MNAR variants and, at HEAD, on the MCAR _60nan variants: 36 cells. The stored E35/E31 cells can't be paired fold by fold (no per-fold lgbm/missForest; E31 has no K).

Readouts:
- model vs bar and missForest per mechanism, on within-variant ratios;
- G-M and column-wise-minus-G under MNAR vs MCAR;
- K-H, the cost of using an oracle checkpoint;
- masked vs induced;
- signed bias per column, from the per-fold ledgers, with no metric-code change.

items.traps:
Real blockers in the stock code:
- Embedding.forward's torch.stack crashes on any table without both column types, which is 7 of 9;
- impute() is transductive only (no new-frame argument), so a fit per population would double the fits to about 630;
- set_random_seed reseeds the global torch/numpy/random streams and the cudnn flags;
- CustomDataset mutates the caller's frame, which would corrupt the cache key (baseline_cache.py:154);
- the wheel pins torch 2.2.2, numpy 1.26.4 and sklearn 1.6.0, so installing it into the fork's venv would downgrade it and change every cache key (baseline_cache.py:82);
- the stock optimizer is Adam without weight decay.
Also: GPU training is not bit-reproducible, so its cache entries are machine-specific. Categorical codes must start at 1. Report that MaCoDE is untuned while TRIDENT is tuned.

items.what:
The LightGbmImputer pattern: subclass GradientBoostingImputer and override _fit_one to return TabPFNRegressor or TabPFNClassifier via create_default_for_version(ModelVersion.V2), with categorical_features_indices. fit, _matrix and impute are inherited: one model per column, a single pass, deterministic mean or argmax fills, on the same cells as the bar.
Three decisions to settle and pre-register:
- drop or keep the hgb recipe's 20% hidden training copy (it pushes pendigits past 10k rows);
- subsample letter (about 11.2k observed rows per column) and electricity (about 25k), or use ignore_pretraining_limits;
- wrap the calls in fork_rng.

Extend item 14's script. Per fold, fit imputers on the training features only. Fill each split through impute(split, hidden=all-False), since existing gaps count as hidden. Then train HGB/LightGBM and RandomForestClassifier(class_weight='balanced'), with and without isna() indicator columns. Arms:
- the paper's own protocol: mode for categoricals, then LightGbmImputer for numericals;
- mean/mode;
- missForest, with fills cached per fold.
Only the 36 gapped variants need imputing.

conflicts_resolved.resolution:
Not a quick win; skip the package. Probe D already reproduced its linear plugins (ICE, SoftImpute) and condexp in numpy, with none of the package's defects:
- three silent plugin bugs (GAIN and SoftImpute ignore their hyperparameters; MIWAE defaults to a 1-unit network);
- the AutoML imputer crashes on sklearn 1.9 (LogisticRegression multi_class);
- transductive fits;
- reseeding of the global streams;
- an upstream dormant since 2023.
What remains unique is the AutoML imputer (10-60 CPU-h, needs stack-and-slice) and GAIN, MIWAE and Sinkhorn, which are known-weak and of low evidence value. It goes to not_quick.

